From 76d2a327eb944cad8a9a80986108f3e9240e19c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:42:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10953/11362] Flag ledger: measured-null is a state, not a
 permanent unevaluated

The ledger's only transition out of `unevaluated` was promotion to `on`
(sweep ~line 564, cmd_promote ~line 589). A flag measured and found NOT
to help recorded its evidence, set promotable: False, and stayed
`unevaluated` forever -- indistinguishable from a flag nobody tested.
Reproduced: 136 flags, 136 unevaluated, 15 with evidence, all 15
promotable: False. The dashboard's "shipped-but-unevaluated" line
conflated a coverage gap (go measure) with a finding (stop spending).

Design (REQ-ARC-FLAG-LEDGER-6862):
- `state_after_measurement(current, ok, why)`: REFUSED/HOLD ->
  `off_measured` (terminal measured-null); UNINTERPRETABLE_* moves
  nothing, because verdict()'s own comments say those measured nothing
  (timed out / lever never took effect) and auto-filing FIRED_NO_EFFECT
  as a null is the exact conflation they forbid; `on` is never demoted
  by bookkeeping. Wired into cmd_measure AND cmd_sweep.
- `--record-null FLAG --note ... --evidence-path ...` records a
  measured null from a run made OUTSIDE the sweep (the r11l tools A/B
  shape). Requires a non-empty note and >=1 existing evidence path,
  records each with sha256, refuses an untracked or promoted flag. The
  r11l result itself is deliberately NOT backfilled -- operator call.
- Dashboard `flag_lines`: "N/M shipped-but-untested, K measured-null",
  UNTESTED and MEASURED-NULL listed separately.

Rejected: mapping UNINTERPRETABLE_FIRED_NO_EFFECT to off_measured
automatically (12 of the 15 evidenced entries) -- distinguishing
"fitted, found nothing to do" from "never fitted" needs fire_counters
reading, which is what --record-null is for.

No migration of the existing 136 entries (operator call). Would-change
count if migrated: 3 under the shipped rule (BOUNDED_REINDUCTION,
GRID_FALLBACK_CANDIDATES, SMALL_OBJECT_FIRST -- latest verdict
REFUSED), 15 under the aggressive rule.

Tests: 6 new in test_arc_bench_and_flag_ledger.py + 2 in
test_outer_loop_dashboard.py. Mutations verified: reverting
off_measured to the old keep-state behavior -> 3 RED; folding
measured-null back into the untested count -> 1 RED; both restored
byte-identical (cmp), suites GREEN. Pre-existing, unrelated:
test_a_numeric_knob_is_never_swept fails at HEAD too (classify_flag
read-site drift).

Mutation-gate marker 9d4b48cf.pending.json deleted deliberately per its
own instructions: its single path is tests/python/test_outer_loop_
dashboard.py, tagged [NOT this run] -- it observed THIS session's
authored edit to that file landing inside a concurrent pytest window,
not test damage.

